2010/7/8 Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com>

> What's wrong with {bancu lo kamvrude jo'u lo kampalci}?
>

I just feel, that the book with "jo'u" is about the distinction between 2
separate entities, while with "jo'e" is about "existence" of (the set of)
both.
In the context of "...no universal morality, that distinguishes...", with
"jo'u"  we still can have the "...universal morality that joins/mixes...",
while with "jo'e" we are denying both.

So with "lo" -- are we speaking about 2 separate entities, or the whole
abstraction of "(.*)ness"?

Alas, I can't say for Nietzsche. I think, here can be 4 significantly
different books with "jo'u lo", "jo'e lo", "jo'u" and "jo'e" between the "
vrude" and "palci".

-- 
mu'o mi'e lex

